/*****************************************************************************
    jitXseq -- TWO value-returning callees, SEQUENTIALLY, NO conjunction.
    2026-08-08. The third and deciding leg of the genKantParse call
    measurement.

    THE THREE RESULTS SO FAR:
        jitXcall  exit 0, degrade 0   one callee, returns NOTHING          green
        jitXret   exit 0, degrade 1   one callee, TAIL return              green
                                      -- green BY TAIL POSITION: E2 says the
                                      unbuilt thing is the BRANCH to the
                                      enclosing epilogue, and a tail return
                                      needs no branch, so falling through is
                                      accidentally equivalent
        jitXand   exit 139, degrade 2 TWO callees with returns, joined by AND

    jitXand varied two things at once. This holds the conjunction out and keeps
    everything else: two inlined callees, each with a tail return, each result
    consumed.

        RED here   ->  the crasher is TWO INLINED VALUE-RETURNING CALLEES in
                       one body, and AND is innocent. That is the worse answer,
                       because the obvious short-circuit rewrite --
                           if !t1(); return 0;
                           if !t2(); return 0;
                       -- has exactly this shape and is blocked too.
        GREEN here ->  the crasher is the CONJUNCTION, and the if-chain rewrite
                       is available today. genKantParse's sequence template can
                       be written with constructs that are already certified.

    THIS IS THE QUESTION THAT DECIDES WHETHER THE SKETCH NEEDS NEW JIT WORK OR
    ONLY A DIFFERENT SPELLING.

    Two fires, inputs changed after emission, answers required to differ.
    SENTINEL AT THE FOOT (H2). Run under a wall-clock cap (H5).
*****************************************************************************/
Start();
include(unitTests);
include(generate);
include(utilities);

search reset stack Grokking;
search Generating UnitTests bcOPs Utilities list;

register(JitXseq);
define
    xsIn;
    xsA;
    xsB;
    xsSum;
    xsTicks;
    xsOne code={
        xsTicks = xsTicks + 1;
        return xsIn * 2;
        };
    xsTwo code={
        xsTicks = xsTicks + 1;
        return xsIn * 3;
        };
    xsDriver code={
        xsA = xsOne();
        xsB = xsTwo();
        xsSum = xsA + xsB;
        };
    ;

xsIn    = 4;
xsA     = 0;
xsB     = 0;
xsSum   = 0;
xsTicks = 0;
print "XS fire 1 setup : xsIn =" xsIn:;
testing(xsDriver);
print "XS fire 1 result: xsA =" xsA " (want 8) xsB =" xsB " (want 12) xsSum =" xsSum " (want 20) ticks =" xsTicks:;

xsIn = 10;
print "XS fire 2 setup : xsIn =" xsIn " (recompile: NONE)":;
jitRefire();
print "XS fire 2 result: xsA =" xsA " (want 20) xsB =" xsB " (want 30) xsSum =" xsSum " (want 50) ticks =" xsTicks:;

xsIn    = 4;
xsA     = 0;
xsB     = 0;
xsSum   = 0;
xsTicks = 0;
xsDriver();
print "XS interpreted  : xsSum =" xsSum " (the oracle -- want 20) ticks =" xsTicks:;

print "XS SENTINEL -- run reached the end":;
stop();
